# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  This repository tracks Python sources and the prompt
#  templates. Nothing else.
#
#  Config, schemas, docs, notebooks, datasets, model weights and
#  every generated artifact stay local. That includes the files
#  the code needs in order to run (pyproject.toml, environment.yml,
#  configs/default.yaml, qa.json), so a fresh clone is source only
#  and will not execute as-is.
#
#  This is an allowlist, not a denylist: ignore everything first,
#  then re-include the two kinds of file we publish. New file
#  types are therefore ignored by default and have to be opted in
#  here deliberately.
#
#  NOTE: gitignore has no end-of-line comments. A `#` only starts
#  a comment at the start of a line, so every comment here sits on
#  its own line.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Ignore everything ───────────────────────────────────────
# `!*/` re-includes directories so git can descend into them.
# Without it git prunes every directory at the top level and the
# re-inclusions below are never reached.
*
!*/

# ── The only tracked content ────────────────────────────────
!*.py
!prompts/*.md
!.gitignore

# ── Re-exclude trees that contain .py files we do not publish ──
# `!*.py` above matches at any depth, so these have to be shut
# out again by name. Rules are last-match-wins, so they must sit
# below the re-inclusions.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
model/
outputs/
outputs_mac_api_before_reference_update/
benchmark/data/
